# Everything moving (calibration/stress scenario)
# Modeled on colloquy/tests/test_light_sensor_values/test_with_everything_moving - a manually-started diagnostic, not something the installation reaches on its own. Male rings are held constant ON here, not blinking a real pattern - treat this as "how long is a female facing a lit male," not a pattern-decode exercise. Default duration is 30 minutes, configurable via params["test with everything moving"]["duration"].

0 Tester starts test_with_everything_moving from the web UI (tests -> test_light_sensor_values -> test_with_everything_moving)
0 Bar moves (blocking) to male1's interaction origin for female1 (move_male1_in_front_of_female1_and_wait())
0 Both male1's and male2's rings are turned on and held steady - not blinking any identity pattern
0 male1.turn_back_and_forth and male2.turn_back_and_forth both start: both males sway independently of any drive/search logic
0 All three females' turn_back_and_forth threads start: female1, female2 and female3 all sway independently
0 bar.turn_back_and_forth starts (full range, not the around-f1 variant): the bar now also sways continuously, on top of the fixed offset it was just moved to
1800 All three female light sensors are read and logged to CSV as one row per tick (seconds, female1, female2, female3) - five bodies plus the bar are all in motion simultaneously for the configured duration (default 1800s/30min)
0 On stop, a TestResults object is built from the accumulated rows for post-hoc plotting - the richest single dataset among the light-sensor test stages, but still only measures sensor/alignment timing, not pattern-decode accuracy
